flowchart TD
    Dequeue([Job dequeued]):::start --> Lease{Lease acquired?}:::decision
    Lease -->|no, already claimed| Drop[Drop duplicate]:::terminal
    Lease -->|yes| Load[(Load draft payload)]:::data
    Load --> Found{Draft found?}:::decision
    Found -->|no| Gone[404 Draft missing]:::error
    Found -->|yes| Cache{Cache hit?}:::decision
    Cache -->|yes| Reuse[Reuse cached artifact]:::process

    subgraph Pool["Render worker pool"]
        direction TB
        Render[Render diagram]:::external
        Attempts{Attempts left?}:::decision
        Backoff[Backoff and requeue]:::async
        Render -->|timeout or error| Attempts
        Attempts -->|yes| Backoff
        Backoff --> Render
    end

    Cache -->|no| Render
    Attempts -->|no| DeadLetter[(Dead-letter job)]:::error
    Render -->|success| Store[(Store artifact)]:::data
    Reuse --> Store
    Store --> Publish[Publish result]:::async
    Publish --> Metrics[Emit metrics]:::filler
    Metrics --> Done([Job complete]):::terminal
    Gone --> Done
    Drop --> Done
    DeadLetter --> Done

    %% Palette: blue-only, same ramp as 01-example-flow.mmd. Hue is constant, so class is carried by lightness.
    classDef start fill:#0d3b66,stroke:#082744,color:#ffffff
    classDef decision fill:#1e6fb8,stroke:#14507f,color:#ffffff
    classDef error fill:#04182c,stroke:#000000,stroke-width:2px,color:#ffffff
    classDef data fill:#2d8fd4,stroke:#1a6aa3,color:#111111
    classDef async fill:#6db3e8,stroke:#3d8fc8,stroke-dasharray:6 3,color:#111111
    classDef process fill:#bcdcf5,stroke:#7fb4dd,color:#111111
    classDef terminal fill:#eaf4fc,stroke:#9ec4e0,color:#111111
    %% `external` and `filler` are deliberately *not* in the blue ramp: they encode a different kind
    %% of node (outside the trust boundary / placeholder), not a step on the lightness ladder. Greys,
    %% so they cannot be mistaken for a ramp step on a colour-only reading.
    classDef external fill:#5c6b7a,stroke:#2f3a45,color:#ffffff
    classDef filler fill:#6e7681,stroke:#484f58,color:#ffffff
